<quiz>
  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>Solving a linear inequality and graphing it on a number line</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>Solve the following inequality for \(x\):</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px;">
\( \displaystyle {@a*x@} + {@b@} < {@c@} \)
</p>

<p><b>a) The algebraic solution:</b></p>
<p><i>(Enter your answer as an inequality. Use <b>&lt;</b> for \(&lt;\). For example, <code>x < 5</code>)</i></p>
<p>Inequality: [[input:ans1]]</p>
<div>[[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</div>

<p><b>b)</b> Represent your solution on the number line below. Drag the blue point to the correct boundary value.</p>
<p><i>(Note: This is a strict inequality, so an open circle is used.)</i></p>

[[jsxgraph input-ref-ans2="rP1" width="550px" height="120px"]]
var brd = JXG.JSXGraph.initBoard(divid, {
    boundingbox: [-7, 2, 7, -2],
    axis: false, grid: false, showNavigation: false, showCopyright: false, pan: {enabled: false}, zoom: {enabled: false}
});


var xaxis = brd.create('axis', [[0, 0], [1, 0]], {
    name: 'x', withLabel: true, label: {position: 'rt', offset: [-5, 15]},
    firstArrow: true, lastArrow: true, strokeWidth: 1.5,
    ticks: {
        drawLabels: true, label: {offset: [0, -15]}, insertTicks: false,
        ticksDistance: 1, minorTicks: 0, majorHeight: 10, drawZero: true
    }
});


var p1 = brd.create('glider', [0, 0, xaxis], {
    name: '', size: 5, strokeColor: '#1565c0', fillColor: '#ffffff', strokeWidth: 2, snapToGrid: true, snapSizeX: 1
});


var pLeft = brd.create('point', [-7, 0], {visible: false});
brd.create('segment', [p1, pLeft], {
    strokeWidth: 4, strokeColor: '#1565c0', highlight: false,
    lastArrow: {type: 1, size: 6}
});


stack_jxg.bind_point(rP1, p1);
stack_jxg.starts_moved(p1);
[[/jsxgraph]]

<div style="display:none">[[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]]</div>
<div>[[feedback:prt2]]</div>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p><b>Worked Solution:</b></p>

<p><b>Part 1: Algebraic Solution</b></p>
<p>To solve the inequality, we need to isolate \(x\).</p>
<p>First, we group the constant terms on the right side by subtracting \({@b@}\) from both sides:</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px;">
\( \displaystyle \begin{aligned}
{@a*x@} &< {@c@} - {@b@} \\
{@a*x@} &< {@c - b@}
\end{aligned} \)
</p>
<p>Next, we divide both sides by the coefficient of \(x\), which is \({@a@}\):</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px;">
\( \displaystyle \begin{aligned}
x &< \frac{{@c - b@}}{{@a@}} \\
x &< {@bound@}
\end{aligned} \)
</p>
<p>Hence, the correct algebraic solution is:</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px;">
\( \displaystyle \boxed{x < {@bound@}} \)
</p>

<p><b>Part 2: Graphical Representation</b></p>
<p>To represent this solution on a number line, we use an <b>open (unshaded) circle</b> at \({@bound@}\) because the inequality is strict (\(<\)). We then shade a thick line extending to the <b>left</b> to represent all numbers less than \({@bound@}\).</p>

[[jsxgraph width="550px" height="120px"]]
var bound = {#bound#};
var brd = JXG.JSXGraph.initBoard(divid, {
    boundingbox: [-7, 2, 7, -2],
    axis: false, grid: false, showNavigation: false, showCopyright: false, pan: {enabled: false}, zoom: {enabled: false}
});


var xaxis = brd.create('axis', [[0, 0], [1, 0]], {
    name: 'x', withLabel: true, label: {position: 'rt', offset: [-5, 15]},
    firstArrow: true, lastArrow: true, strokeWidth: 1.5,
    ticks: {
        drawLabels: true, label: {offset: [0, -15]}, insertTicks: false,
        ticksDistance: 1, minorTicks: 0, majorHeight: 10, drawZero: true
    }
});


var p1 = brd.create('point', [bound, 0], {visible: false});
var pLeft = brd.create('point', [-7, 0], {visible: false});
brd.create('segment', [p1, pLeft], {
    strokeWidth: 4, strokeColor: '#1565c0', highlight: false,
    lastArrow: {type: 1, size: 6}
});


brd.create('point', [bound, 0], {name: '', size: 5, strokeColor: '#1565c0', fillColor: '#ffffff', strokeWidth: 2, fixed: true, highlight: false});
[[/jsxgraph]]]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
